// The look (docs/design.md, "Forms" and "The picture"): a function from a place on a form to what
// its surface wears there. An author writes what is worn and never light, bands or ink; those are
// the one shading function's (`shade::lit`), in the game's style.
//
// Every field of `Skin` but `emits` is one that the look drawn today reads: `rywible/wrela` at
// 7ae6711e, content/humanoid/fighter.wrela `painted` (745-820), content/hakuro/hakuro.wrela
// `Cloth` (26-33) and `dressed` (1251-1264). `emits` is for spells, which that look never had.

/// Where on a form a look is asked.
pub struct Place: Copy {
    /// The point in the world, as the form stands now.
    pub world: vec3,
    /// The same point at rest, before anything posed or moved it: what a garment's pattern
    /// follows, so it stays on the cloth as the cloth moves.
    pub rest: vec3,
    /// The place on its chart (`kinds::Chart`), where the form has one: a limb's way along and
    /// angle round, a sheet's or a height's two numbers. None for the other kinds.
    pub chart: Option<vec2>,
    /// The unit normal out of the surface.
    pub normal: vec3,
}

/// What a surface wears at a place.
pub struct Skin: Copy + GpuData {
    /// Its colour, linear. (Today's palette was chosen on the screen and raised to 2.2 when drawn,
    /// fighter.wrela:765; a look gives the raised colour.)
    pub albedo: vec3,
    /// The line field: ink is drawn where its sign changes. Today it is the cloth's value less
    /// 0.14, so the edge between dark and pale cloth is a line (fighter.wrela:800).
    pub line: f32,
    /// How much it is metal: over a half, it glints where it turns to the sun (gold;
    /// fighter.wrela:776-779, hakuro.wrela:29).
    pub metal: f32,
    /// Whether the rim light falls on it. Off where a sheet seen along itself would be all edge:
    /// today the coat's tails (fighter.wrela:785-789).
    pub rim: bool = true,
    /// How far it stands off the form (m): a seam's welt, a rib, a weave. Too fine to be a side of
    /// the form, it is seen by how it tilts the light (hakuro.wrela:30-32, 1258).
    pub relief: f32 = 0.0,
    /// What it gives off, linear, added unshaded: a rune, a charged blade, a spell's core where
    /// it is a surface. None by default. (Today's look has nothing that emits; spells will.)
    pub emits: vec3 = vec3(),
    /// Two numbers from 0 to 1 a look keeps for its finish (`Look::finished`): on a solid that
    /// wears its look from its cook, baked at each vertex with the rest of the skin and laid
    /// between the corners, so the finish at a pixel reads them from `baked` and need not work
    /// them out again (what is near, how far in). Nothing else reads them.
    pub kept: vec2 = vec2(),
}

/// A look: what a form's surface wears at each place. Plain data, as the kinds are, so one look
/// runs on the CPU and reaches the GPU as a uniform.
pub trait Look: Copy + GpuData {
    /// What is worn at `at`.
    fn skin(self, at: Place) -> Skin

    /// Whether what it wears may be worked out no finer than the surface it is on is drawn (a
    /// lister's vertices, laid between them), not at each pixel: its detail is coarser than a
    /// triangle where the surface stands (8 pixels: `atoms::mesh`), it doesn't change in time,
    /// and on a copy that moves it doesn't depend on where in the world the copy is. A look
    /// says so; none is taken to.
    fn coarse(self) -> bool {
        false
    }

    /// Whether, on a solid that wears this look from its cook (`atoms::mesh::bake_mesh_worn`:
    /// its skin worked out at each vertex when the game is built), the triangles round `at` want
    /// detail finer than their corners carry: those, and only those, run `finished` at each
    /// pixel. Asked at the cook, never in a frame. None by default: a look baked is wholly baked.
    fn fine(self, at: Place) -> bool {
        false
    }

    /// On a solid that wears this look from its cook and is placed many times (the cook works it
    /// out in the solid's own space), what one copy changes of the skin baked at a corner: a
    /// tint, say, so copies of one solid differ. Worked out at each corner each frame, so it is
    /// to be cheap, and it never asks the form. By default the baked skin.
    fn copied(self, baked: Skin) -> Skin {
        baked
    }

    /// The skin at a pixel of a triangle `fine` marked, given `baked` (the skin baked at its
    /// corners, laid between them, with what the look kept there: `Skin::kept`): what the look
    /// adds there that is finer than the corners, from `baked` and the pixel's place, never
    /// asking the form. By default, the baked skin.
    fn finished(self, baked: Skin, at: Place) -> Skin {
        baked
    }
}

/// What a medium does with light at a place, a unit of its density's worth (its density is how
/// much of it a ray meets per metre): a medium has no surface to wear a skin, so this is its
/// look's answer. An author gives colours, never light: how it is lit is the one shading
/// function's (`shade::scattered`).
pub struct Mist: Copy + GpuData {
    /// The colour of the light it scatters, linear: white water's near 1, none for a glow that
    /// only gives light.
    pub albedo: vec3,
    /// How much brighter it is seen looking toward the sun through it than across: a forward
    /// lobe's peak over its floor (spray's 10: rywible/wrela scenes/opening/paint.wrela at
    /// 7ae6711e, :1788-1790). 0, none.
    pub forward: f32,
    /// What it gives off, linear, unshaded: a spell's glow.
    pub emits: vec3,
}

/// A medium's look: what it does with light at each place, given its density there. Plain
/// data, as `Look` is.
pub trait Haze: Copy + GpuData {
    /// What it does with light at `at`, where its density is `density`.
    fn mist(self, at: vec3, density: f32) -> Mist
}
